  {
    "description": "Decide something waiting on the user, named by the ref a list or get result gave (or its position in the last result): approve or reject (accept and discard for a draft or a runbook proposal), or deliver an approved change. The user confirms on a card that shows what it is (with its amount where it has one) and may flip the decision or add a note there. Never a name: list what is waiting first. Here it decides: hitl-approval, a pending transaction (approve or reject; the card shows its amount); change, an agent change (approve, reject, or deliver once approved); runbook-proposal, a runbook proposal (accept or reject; a rejection needs a note); proposal, a graph change proposal (approve or reject); consult, a computer's consult (approve, with the answer as the note); design, a design thread (approve or reject the sign-off).",
    "name": "decide",
